index 0000000..f6876d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/vision/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# DeiT-Tiny / ImageNet-1k
+
+Patch 072 adds an independent image-classification entrypoint. It aims to reproduce
+the **non-distilled DeiT-Tiny 72.2% ImageNet-1k top-1 result**; that result has not
+been reproduced here. Text training, tokenization, generation and language
+benchmarks are unchanged.
+
+The reference is the [2021 DeiT implementation](https://github.com/facebookresearch/deit/tree/ab5715372db8c6cad5740714b2216d55aeae052e)
+and [published result](https://github.com/facebookresearch/deit/blob/ab5715372db8c6cad5740714b2216d55aeae052e/README.md).
+The architecture has 5,717,416 parameters: 224-pixel input, 16-pixel patches,
+192 hidden dimensions, 12 layers, 3 attention heads, GELU MLP ratio 4, LayerNorm,
+learned absolute positions and a CLS classification head. Attention is global
+and non-causal. `forward_features` returns CLS plus all image tokens; this patch
+does not add a vision-language model or pretrained/distilled weights.
+
+## Dependencies and data
+
+Use the existing CUDA/PyTorch image with a **working torchvision build matching
+that exact PyTorch/CUDA build**, NumPy and Pillow. The language-model image's
+nightly PyTorch must not be replaced by a dependency resolver. Install the pinned
+vision helper library without changing the image's Torch stack:
+
+```bash
+python -m pip install --no-deps -r experiments/vision/requirements.txt
+```
+
+This uses modern timm for augmentation, repeated-augmentation sampling, Mixup,
+EMA and the scheduler. It does not import timm's model implementation. The old
+reference used timm 0.3.2, which depends on APIs removed from modern PyTorch.
+The installed timm/torchvision/Pillow/PyTorch versions are recorded in each run.
+
+Obtain ImageNet-1k separately under its dataset terms. There are no automatic
+dataset or checkpoint downloads. Supply extracted images in ImageFolder layout:
+
+```text
+/data/imagenet/
+    train/n01440764/*.JPEG
+    train/n01443537/*.JPEG
+    ...
+    val/n01440764/*.JPEG
+    val/n01443537/*.JPEG
+    ...
+```
+
+Both splits must have the same 1,000 class directories. The official validation
+archive needs organizing into these class directories using its ground-truth
+labels. The full reference dataset has 1,281,167 training and 50,000 validation
+images; the actual counts are logged. Using a subset is a functional check,
+not a reproduction of the published accuracy.
+
+## Run
+
+From the repository with patch 072 applied, single-GPU training is:
+
+```bash
+nohup python -u train_vision.py --data-path /data/imagenet \
+    > vision-training.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &
+```
+
+The default microbatch is 256 with four accumulation steps, giving effective
+batch 1,024. Lower `--batch-size` to an even divisor of 1,024 if needed. The
+reference four-GPU batch arrangement uses no accumulation:
+
+```bash
+nohup torchrun --standalone --nproc_per_node=4 train_vision.py \
+    --data-path /data/imagenet --batch-size 256 --global-batch-size 1024 \
+    > vision-training.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &
+```
+
+Run configurations live in `config/vision.py`; main architecture and execution
+settings also have `--help` options. Default precision is FP16 autocast with a
+gradient scaler and FP32 parameters/AdamW states. `--precision bf16` and
+`--precision fp32` are separate numerical experiments. `--attention-backend sdpa`
+is the default; `--attention-backend flex` uses compiled FlexAttention over all
+image tokens, without a causal or text-document mask. Both routes use the same
+projections and model. Flex attention dropout is unsupported and explicitly
+rejected. `--compile` additionally compiles the complete model.
+
+The recipe uses AdamW, base LR 5e-4 scaled by effective batch / 512, weight decay
+0.05 excluding bias/norm/CLS/position parameters, five warmup epochs from 1e-6,
+cosine minimum LR 1e-5, 300 epochs, stochastic depth 0.1, Mixup 0.8, CutMix 1.0,
+label smoothing 0.1, RandAugment `rand-m9-mstd0.5-inc1`, pixel random erasing 0.25,
+repeated augmentation 3 and EMA decay 0.99996. Validation resizes the short side
+to 256 then center-crops 224; disjoint distributed shards count each image once.
+
+The historical reference calls `scheduler.step(epoch)` **after** training each
+zero-indexed epoch. This ordering is preserved, including epochs 0 and 1 starting
+at the warmup initial LR. Although the old scheduler factory returned 310 epochs
+including cooldown, DeiT ignored that return and trained 300; no extra cooldown
+epochs are added. Shortening `epochs` changes the cosine schedule and is not the
+reference recipe.
+
+Accumulation matches the effective update batch size, but one GPU does not
+reproduce the four-GPU augmentation grouping, sampler interleaving or RNG
+trajectory. The final incomplete accumulation group uses its actual microbatch
+count. Modern PyTorch/SDPA, torchvision, Pillow and timm also introduce numerical
+or augmentation differences from the 2021 stack. A 72.2% result is a target to
+measure, not a promised outcome. Report ordinary-model top-1 separately from
+EMA top-1; the implementation never silently selects the better of the two.
+
+## Results, checkpoints and the Hub
+
+The printed `configs_and_logs/vision-TIMESTAMP` directory contains `config.json`,
+`source.txt`, `log.txt`, per-epoch `metrics.jsonl`, `status.json`, `latest.pth` and
+the best ordinary-model `best.pth`. Metrics include raw/EMA top-1 and top-5,
+losses, processed images, train/validation durations and cumulative times.
+Checkpoints retain model, EMA, AdamW, scaler, scheduler and per-rank RNG states.
+Resume is at epoch boundaries with the same world size, batch and recipe:
+
+```bash
+python -u train_vision.py --data-path /data/imagenet \
+    --resume /root/gpt-moe/configs_and_logs/vision-TIMESTAMP/latest.pth
+```
+
+Evaluation of your own local checkpoint is:
+
+```bash
+python -u train_vision.py --data-path /data/imagenet --eval \
+    --resume /root/gpt-moe/configs_and_logs/vision-TIMESTAMP/best.pth
+```
+
+The trainer needs no Hub credentials unless `--upload-hf` is supplied. With
+`HF_USER` and `HF_TOKEN` (or their lowercase counterparts) already exported, add
+`--upload-hf` to create a new `HF_USER/deit-tiny_TIMESTAMP` repository containing
+the run directory, including both checkpoints. Catchable training failures also
+upload available logs; training errors keep their nonzero exit status. A hard
+kill or destroyed instance cannot run this final upload. SIGTERM is handled
+gracefully and attempts this final upload, but does not create a mid-epoch
+checkpoint; `latest.pth` remains the most recent completed epoch. Each checkpoint is
+approximately 90 MB for the reference model; the uploaded folder contains two.
+Upload failures are printed and return a nonzero exit status. Credentials are
+not written to configuration or source logs.
+
+To follow progress:
+
+```bash
+tail -n 50 -f vision-training.log
+```
